# Frozen 2026-09-04: functions whose LAST statement is a conditional, reviewed and
# KEPT because the caller reads that status as an answer, never as success. Two-way:
# a frozen function that stops ending on a conditional is STALE and its line goes.
# Format: <file>\t<function>.
# docs/code-quality-tooling.md#trailing-conditional-returns-trailing-conditional

# Pure predicates. Every call site is a condition (`if f`, `f || return 0`,
# `f && x`), so a false answer is the point and returning 1 is the contract.
# cross_build_is_active ends on a CALL to the frozen cross_target_is_foreign, and
# is_cross/cross_build_enabled are its one-line aliases: three rows for one body.
linux/scripts/01-core/context-management.sh	runtime_pushes_intermediate_images
linux/scripts/01-core/context-management.sh	runtime_use_local_stage_context_outputs
linux/scripts/01-core/cross-apt.sh	is_cross_riscv64
linux/scripts/03-media/build/onnxruntime/build/lib/common.sh	is_amd64_arch

# Verdict functions: the trailing test IS the verdict, and a caller that wants the
# "nothing happened" arm spells it out. smoke_test_ffmpeg fails the build when a
# codec probe failed; patch_csound_sys_char_signedness answers "did I patch
# anything", and both its callers say so (`|| true` at :511, `&& retry` at :522).

